warming|getting-warmer|NOUN|rise in temperature|The process of becoming warmer or increasing in temperature.|sự nóng lên; sự ấm lên|The warming of the room was gradual after the heater came on.|Căn phòng ấm dần lên sau khi máy sưởi bật.|Uncountable process noun; warming of names what becomes warmer. Global warming is a specific context rather than the only meaning.|0
driver|vehicle-operator|NOUN|person operating a vehicle|A person who controls a car or other road vehicle while it is moving.|người lái xe; tài xế|The driver waited until everyone had fastened their seat belt.|Tài xế chờ cho đến khi mọi người thắt dây an toàn.|Countable; driver of a vehicle names the person operating it, not every passenger.|0
homogeneous|uniform-composition|ADJECTIVE|similar throughout in composition|Having the same or very similar composition or characteristics throughout.|đồng nhất; tương đối đồng đều|Stir the mixture until it looks homogeneous.|Khuấy hỗn hợp cho đến khi trông đồng nhất.|Before a noun or after a linking verb; homogeneity concerns uniform composition, not moral agreement.|-
indifferent|uninterested|ADJECTIVE|showing little concern|Not showing interest or concern about someone or something.|thờ ơ; không quan tâm|He seemed indifferent to the choice of restaurant.|Anh ấy có vẻ không quan tâm đến việc chọn nhà hàng.|Indifferent to names what causes little interest; this sense does not necessarily mean actively hostile.|-
radio|receiver|NOUN|device receiving sound broadcasts|A device that receives broadcasts of speech or music.|đài phát thanh; máy radio|She turned the radio down so she could hear the knock.|Cô ấy vặn nhỏ tiếng đài để nghe tiếng gõ cửa.|Countable for the device; turn the radio down reduces volume, not its physical position.|0
radio|broadcast-medium|NOUN|broadcasting of sound programmes|The medium of broadcasting sound programmes to listeners.|phát thanh; radio|The interview will be broadcast on local radio tomorrow.|Cuộc phỏng vấn sẽ được phát trên đài địa phương vào ngày mai.|Usually uncountable; on the radio refers to broadcast availability rather than a device's surface.|0
